Worker
======

Worker is a dynamically configured application server.  It runs application
code in multiple language runtimes and manages application processes through a
JSON control API.

Worker can serve HTTP traffic directly with request routing,
or run behind a reverse proxy.

Building
--------

Configure and build the core daemon:

    ./configure
    make

Configure the language modules required by your applications before running
make.  For example:

    ./configure python
    ./configure php
    ./configure ruby

The daemon is built as `build/workerd`.  Start it in the foreground with a
local control socket:

    mkdir -p build/state
    build/workerd --no-daemon --modules build --state build/state \
        --pid build/worker.pid --log build/worker.log --tmp /tmp \
        --control unix:/tmp/control.worker.sock

Worker configuration is read and changed over the control API.  The following
example starts a Python WSGI application on port 8080:

    curl -X PUT --data-binary @- \
        --unix-socket /tmp/control.worker.sock \
        http://localhost/config/ <<'EOF'
    {
        "listeners": {
            "127.0.0.1:8080": {
                "pass": "applications/example"
            }
        },
        "applications": {
            "example": {
                "type": "python",
                "path": "/srv/example",
                "module": "wsgi"
            }
        }
    }
    EOF

